Cell 93 defines the acc() function that is used throughout the notebook to evaluate model performance (Cells 104, 117, 139, 152, 164). The function is fundamentally broken:

def acc(coeffs):
    preds = calc_preds(coeffs, trn_indep).flatten()
    keep = torch.rand(preds.shape[0], device=preds.device) > 0.1
    return (trn_dep.flatten()[keep].bool()==(preds[keep]>torch.rand_like(preds[keep]))).float().mean()

The function generates random threshold values via `torch.rand_like(preds[keep])` and compares predictions against these random values instead of the actual ground truth labels `trn_dep`.
